  grh-ln "      <h3><span class='ep' data-pure='Exact Signed/Rational Rings &amp; Multiplicative Divisor Inversion' data-wb='Dirichlet Convolution Ring, M&ouml;bius Inversion, von Mangoldt Weights &amp; Mertens Bound'>Exact Signed/Rational Rings &amp; Multiplicative Divisor Inversion</span></h3>" (
  grh-ln "      <p>Taking the logarithmic derivative of the prime-factorized product <span class='m'>&prod;<sub><i>p</i></sub>(1 &minus; &chi;(<i>p</i>)<i>p</i><sup>&minus;<i>s</i></sup>)<sup>&minus;1</sup></span> converts prime factorization into an additive <span class='ep' data-pure='multiplicative scale series' data-wb='Dirichlet series'>multiplicative scale series</span> supported strictly on prime powers <span class='m'><i>p</i><sup><i>k</i></sup></span> weighted by the <span class='ep' data-pure='prime-power logarithmic indicator' data-wb='von Mangoldt function'>prime-power logarithmic indicator</span> <span class='m'>&Lambda;(<i>n</i>)</span>.</p>" (
  grh-ln "      <p>Under <span class='ep' data-pure='multiplicative divisor convolution' data-wb='Dirichlet convolution'>multiplicative divisor convolution</span> <span class='m'>(<i>f</i> &lowast; <i>g</i>)(<i>n</i>) = &sum;<sub><i>d</i>|<i>n</i></sub> <i>f</i>(<i>d</i>)<i>g</i>(<i>n</i>/<i>d</i>)</span>, the <span class='ep' data-pure='squarefree parity sign' data-wb='M&ouml;bius function'>squarefree parity sign</span> <span class='m'>&mu;(<i>n</i>) &isin; {&minus;1, 0, +1}</span> is the exact convolution inverse of the constant unit <span class='m'>1(<i>n</i>) = 1</span>. Therefore <span class='m'>1/<i>L</i>(<i>s</i>, &chi;) = &sum;<sub><i>n</i>&ge;1</sub> &mu;(<i>n</i>)&chi;(<i>n</i>)<i>n</i><sup>&minus;<i>s</i></sup></span> is analytic on <span class='m'>&Re;(<i>s</i>) &gt; 1/2</span> if and only if <span class='ep' data-pure='cumulative parity sums' data-wb='Mertens sums'>cumulative parity sums</span> cancel at square-root scale.</p>" (
  grh-ln "      <div class='eq'>&minus;<i>L</i>&prime;(<i>s</i>, &chi;) / <i>L</i>(<i>s</i>, &chi;) = &sum;<sub><i>n</i>&ge;1</sub> &Lambda;(<i>n</i>)&chi;(<i>n</i>)<i>n</i><sup>&minus;<i>s</i></sup>, &emsp; (&mu; &lowast; 1)(<i>n</i>) = [<i>n</i> = 1], &emsp; &prod;<sub><i>d</i> | <i>n</i></sub> &Lambda;<sub>base</sub>(<i>d</i>) = <i>n</i></div>" (
