  grh-ln "      <h3><span class='ep' data-pure='Unitary Harmonic Involution, Subgroup&ndash;Annihilator Sum &amp; Origin-Zeroing Space' data-wb='Schwartz&ndash;Bruhat Space, Pontryagin / Walsh&ndash;Hadamard Transform, Poisson&ndash;Riemann&ndash;Roch, Plancherel &amp; Masullo B_0'>Unitary Harmonic Involution, Subgroup&ndash;Annihilator Sum &amp; Origin-Zeroing Space</span></h3>" (
  grh-ln "      <p>The reflection <span class='m'><i>s</i> &harr; 1 &minus; <i>s</i></span> originates from <span class='ep' data-pure='self-dual character transformation' data-wb='Pontryagin&ndash;Tate Fourier duality'>self-dual character transformation</span> <span class='m'>&Fscr;</span> on <span class='ep' data-pure='rapid-decay locally constant test functions' data-wb='Schwartz&ndash;Bruhat spaces'>rapid-decay locally constant test functions</span>. Over exact rationals, <span class='m'>&Fscr;</span> satisfies both <span class='ep' data-pure='unitary l2 energy conservation' data-wb='Plancherel&ndash;Parseval unitarity'>unitary l2 energy conservation</span> and the <span class='ep' data-pure='subgroup&ndash;annihilator dual sum identity' data-wb='Poisson&ndash;Riemann&ndash;Roch summation formula'>subgroup&ndash;annihilator dual sum identity</span> <span class='m'>&Theta;<sub><i>f</i></sub>(1) + <i>f</i>(0) = &Theta;<sub>&Fscr;<i>f</i></sub>(1) + (&Fscr;<i>f</i>)(0)</span>.</p>" (
